--- body ---

## Context

`bin/idh` exists (`adapters/perch.py`, 512 lines, ticket 0802) with `install`,
`uninstall`, `status`, `relocate` and `check` — but only for skill discovery.
It is not on PATH, not documented in the README, and called by path from two
scripts. Every other lifecycle job has its own entry point:

| Job | Today |
|---|---|
| Skills visible to each runtime | `idh install/uninstall/status` |
| Hooks, settings, config links | `adapters/install-wirings.sh` |
| Pre-launch link check | `scripts/validate-projections.py` (0983) |
| `~/.bashrc` loader block | copied by hand from `scripts/bashrc-loader.sh` |
| Timers | `bin/install-cron`, `scripts/install-mammoth-audit-timer.sh`, `claude-refresh` unit |
| Checkout update | `scripts/sync-local-main.sh`, `claude-harness-pull` |
| Relocation | none yet (0985/0986) |

`install-wirings.sh` and `adapters/projections.json` keep two separate lists of
links, which can drift.

## Decision (author, 2026-09-29)

Three layers, each with one job:

1. **The author, managing a machine** — `idh install | check | status | sync | relocate`.
   Installed by `~/.idh/bin/idh install`, which also links itself into
   `~/.local/bin/idh`. On a new host: clone, then that one command.
2. **The runtimes (hooks, skills, gates)** — keep calling scripts by direct path
   under `~/.idh/scripts/`. Not routed through `idh`: that would add a single
   point of failure and startup cost to every hook.
3. **The rescue path** — the refusing stubs in the `~/.bashrc` loader block and
   the printed `ln -sfn` repairs. Must work when `~/.idh` itself is broken, so it
   never depends on `idh`.

Optional: git-style dispatch (`idh foo` runs `scripts/idh-foo`) for occasional
manual scripts; author convenience only.

## Constraints

- A merge, not a new layer (harness cool-down): each old entry point is deleted as
  its job moves into `idh`. If the first pass does not shrink the total, stop and
  report.
- `projections.json` is the one list: `idh install` creates exactly what `idh check`
  verifies.
- Codex hooks: an untrusted or changed definition silently runs no guard; any
  change to `adapters/codex/hooks.json` needs a `/hooks` re-trust and a fresh
  `codex exec` block probe in the same step.
- Read what the existing `idh relocate` does before extending it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `~/.idh/bin/idh install` on a disposable HOME installs skills, wirings, the loader block and timers from `projections.json`, and links `~/.local/bin/idh`; `idh check` passes right after (positive control), and fails with a named culprit after one planted broken link (negative control)
- [ ] `install-wirings.sh`, `bin/install-cron`, the timer installer and the manual loader copy are removed or reduced to a one-line call to `idh`; net line count of the replaced entry points goes down
- [ ] `idh sync` fast-forwards the checkout and, when it cannot, names the blocking files (the padme case of 2026-09-29)
- [ ] `idh status` reports installed vs declared and distance to origin
- [ ] README installation section is the two-command bootstrap
- [ ] Hooks and skills still call scripts by path; no hook routes through `idh`
- [ ] `make check` passes
